WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.875
The lab runs in a test tenant, never
production, and the authors haven't run it.

2
00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:09.125
You need Module 2's lab done and
an Internet Access test license.

3
00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:13.237
Step one finds the internet profile
with Learn's filtered request,

4
00:00:13.237 --> 00:00:16.825
enables it, and assigns the
pilot group in the admin center.

5
00:00:16.825 --> 00:00:19.278
Step two creates the filtering policy,

6
00:00:19.278 --> 00:00:23.187
blocking Learn's example
category, artificial intelligence.

7
00:00:23.187 --> 00:00:26.260
Step three creates the
pilot security profile

8
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.938
and links the policy to
it, with logging on.

9
00:00:28.938 --> 00:00:32.537
Step four assigns the profile
with Conditional Access,

10
00:00:32.537 --> 00:00:35.901
scoped to the pilot, with
emergency access excluded.

11
00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:39.698
Step five tests it: on the
pilot device, as a pilot user,

12
00:00:39.698 --> 00:00:43.937
browse to a site in that category
and expect the block page.

13
00:00:43.937 --> 00:00:46.671
Then the guide's traffic
query in the workspace

14
00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:49.540
should show a denied count
on the pilot user's row.
